id: 38
hanzi: 讽刺
pinyin: fěng cì
level: HSK 5
part_of_speech: Verb/Noun

meanings_summary:
  en: to satirize; mock; sarcasm; irony
  es: satirizar; burlarse de; ironía; sarcasmo

senses[1]{sense_number,part_of_speech,register,definition_en,definition_es,example_phrase}:
  1 | Verb | Standard | to criticize, ridicule, or mock through witty irony or caustic metaphor | criticar, ridiculizar o censurar mediante ironía ingeniosa o metáfora mordaz | 辛辣讽刺 (pungent satire)

example_sentences[2]{id,hanzi,pinyin,en,es}:
  #1 | 后世史学家常以“纸上谈兵”这一典故，深刻讽刺那些空谈高深理论而缺乏实践检验的夸夸其谈之辈。 | Hòushì shǐxuéjiā cháng yǐ 'zhǐshàng-tánbīng' zhè yí diǎngù, shēnkè fěngcì nàxiē kōngtán gāoshēn lǐlùn ér quēfá shíjiàn jiǎnyàn de kuākuā-qítán zhī bèi. | Later historians frequently cited the idiom 'armchair strategy' to sharply satirize those braggarts who preach lofty theories without practical testing. | Los historiadores posteriores utilizaron el modismo 'estrategia en el papel' para satirizar a quienes predican elevadas teorías sin haberlas puesto a prueba en la realidad.
  #2 | 这部文学杰作运用了极其辛辣的幽默讽刺手法，无情揭示了当年封建官僚体制的虚伪与腐朽。 | Zhè bù wénxué jiézuò yùnyòng le jíqí xīnlà de yōumò fěngcì shǒufǎ, wúqíng jiēshì le dāngnián fēngjiàn guānliáo tǐzhì de xūwěi yǔ fǔxiǔ. | This literary masterpiece employed pungent humorous satire, ruthlessly exposing the hypocrisy and decay of the feudal bureaucratic system. | Esta obra maestra literaria empleó una sátira sumamente mordaz, desnudando sin piedad la hipocresía y corrupción de la burocracia feudal.

collocations[6]{hanzi,en}:
  辛辣讽刺 | pungent / biting satire
  充满讽刺 | full of irony / satire
  讽刺小说 | satirical novel
  讽刺意味 | satirical undertone
  加以讽刺 | subject to ridicule / satirize
  幽默讽刺 | humorous irony

idioms[4]{hanzi,pinyin,meaning_en}:
  冷嘲热讽 | lěng cháo rè fěng | scoffing and jeering; cynical mockery and burning satire
  指桑骂槐 | zhǐ sāng mà huái | point at the mulberry and scold the locust tree; criticize indirectly
  拐弯抹角 | guǎi wān mò jiǎo | speak in circumlocutions; beat around the bush
  尖酸刻薄 | jiān suān kè bó | sharp and biting; caustic and acerbic

character_decomposition[2]{character,pinyin,meaning_en,meaning_es,radical,radical_meaning_en,meaning_component,sound_component,stroke_count,composition_type,etymology_and_mnemonic,visual_mnemonic_story_en,visual_mnemonic_story_es,tone_mnemonic_anchor,cangjie,traditional}:
  讽 | fěng | satirize; mock; chant; recite | satirizar; burlarse de; recitar; censurar | 讠 | speech / words | 讠 (speech / words) + 风 (wind / indirect influence) | 风 (fēng) | 8 | 左右结构 | Spoken words 讠 delivered indirectly like gentle wind 风 to critique flaws; denotes indirect satire. | Delivering spoken words (讠) like a sharp gust of wind (风) to criticize obliquely (讽). | Pronunciar palabras (讠) como una ráfaga de viento (风) que censura indirectamente (讽). | 214 | IVHN | 諷
  刺 | cì | thorn; prick; pierce; sting; assassinate | espina; pinchar; punzar; picar; asesinar | 刂 | knife / blade | 朿 (brambles / thorns) + 刂 (sharp knife blade) | 朿 (cì) | 8 | 左右结构 | A thorny bramble 朿 combined with a sharp knife 刂; signifies pricking, stabbing, and stinging critique. | A thorny plant (朿) with the sharpness of a knife (刂) that pricks and stings (刺). | Una zarza espinosa (朿) tan punzante como una cuchilla (刂) que pincha y escuece (刺). | 51 | DBLN | 刺

mnemonics_and_roots:
  composite_memory_hook_en: Words delivered obliquely like wind (讽) designed to prick like sharp thorns (刺) deliver biting satire (讽刺).
  composite_memory_hook_es: Palabras que soplan como viento (讽) y pinchan como afiladas espinas (刺) crean la sátira (讽刺).
  cultural_and_cognitive_roots: Rooted in classical poetic traditions (Feng) of remonstrating with emperors through subtle allegories.
  tone_sandhi_and_pitch_modulation: Third tone to fourth tone: 'fěng cì' (214-51). Half-third dip rising before falling sharply on 'cì'.

traps_and_cognates:
  look_alikes[4]{character,pinyin,meaning_en,distinction_note}:
    风 | fēng | wind; custom | No speech 讠 radical on left
