    枣 | zǎo | jujube; date | Double 朿 without knife radical 刂
    策 | cè | policy; strategy | Bamboo ⺮ radical on top
  etymological_cognates[4]{character,pinyin,gloss_en}:
    讥讽 | jīfěng | taunt; deride; mock
    讽喻 | fěngyù | parable; moral allegory
    刺耳 | cì'ěr | grating; harsh on the ears
    刺激 | cìjī | stimulate; excite; provoke

semantic_boundary_contrasts:
  core_nuance: 讽刺 uses witty, ironic, or metaphoric critique to pierce and expose hypocrisy, vice, or incompetence.
  contrasts[3]{id,compared_word,pinyin,analysis}:
    1 | 讽刺 vs. 嘲笑 | cháoxiào | 嘲笑 denotes direct teasing or derisive laughter, whereas 讽刺 relies on artistic or literary irony with moral critique.
    2 | 讽刺 vs. 批评 | pīpíng | 批评 is straightforward evaluation pointing out shortcomings, whereas 讽刺 conveys disapproval through irony and sting.
    3 | 讽刺 vs. 挖苦 | wāku | 挖苦 refers to colloquial, petty barbs aimed at hurting someone's feelings, whereas 讽刺 often carries broader social critique.

extended_reading_passages[2]{id,hanzi,pinyin,en,es}:
  #1 | “纸上谈兵”作为流传两千余年的著名成语，不仅记录了长平之战的悲惨结局，更成为汉语中讽刺脱离实际、夸夸其谈的经典隐喻。这种鞭辟入里的历史讽刺，始终警醒着后人必须尊崇实践，切勿自欺欺人。 | 'Zhǐshàng-tánbīng' zuòwéi liúchuán liǎng qiān yú nián de zhùmíng chéngyǔ, bùjǐn jìlù le Chángpíng zhī zhàn de bēicǎn jiéjú, gèng chéngwéi Hànyǔ zhōng fěngcì tuōlí shíjì, kuākuā-qítán de jīngdiǎn yǐnyù. Zhè zhǒng biānpì-rùlǐ de lìshǐ fěngcì, shǐzhōng jǐngxǐng zhe hòurén bìxū zūnchóng shíjiàn, qièwù zìqī-qīrén. | Passing down for two millennia, 'armchair strategy' not only chronicles Changping's tragedy but serves as Chinese's classic satire against impractical talkers. This piercing historical irony cautions us to honor practice and never deceive ourselves. | Con más de dos milenios de historia, 'estrategia en el papel' no solo narra la tragedia de Changping, sino que es la gran sátira china contra quienes teorizan sin base. Esta aguda ironía nos recuerda priorizar la práctica y evitar el autoengaño.
  #2 | 讽刺艺术向来被誉为社会改良的有力思想武器。无论古代寓言还是现代先锋戏剧，创作者借助精妙的隐喻与讽刺笔触，能够以幽默的形式直击时代弊病，唤醒沉睡的大众心灵，促使全社会反思并不断革故鼎新。 | Fěngcì yìshù xiànglái bèi yù wéi shèhuì gǎiliáng de yǒulì sīxiǎng wǔqì. Wúlùn gǔdài yùyán háishì xiàndài xiānfēng xìjù, chuàngzuòzhě jièzhù jīngmiào de yǐnyù yǔ fěngcì bǐchù, nénggòu yǐ yōumò de xíngshì zhíjī shídài bìbìng, huànxǐng chénshuì de dàzhòng xīnlíng, cùshǐ quán shèhuì fǎnsī bìng bùduàn gégù-dǐngxīn. | The art of satire has long been hailed as an intellectual weapon for social reform. In fables or avant-garde drama, through witty metaphor and satire, artists critique social ills and awaken public conscience to inspire reform. | El arte satírico ha sido considerado un instrumento de mejora social. Tanto en fábulas como en el teatro contemporáneo, mediante metáforas ingeniosas los autores exponen las dolencias de su época para impulsar una constante renovación cívica.
